en:
My name is Reiko Fukuzawa.
I'm in Cla-a-ass 1-G!
The story I'm going to tell is about the swim club.{p}

Don't worry. The club room lock opens with a bit of wire.
I'm good at this kind of thing.
...Keep it a secret, okay?{p}

...Okay, we're going in.
There's no practice today.
Nobody's here, trust me.{p}

The locker just sat there, silent.
No different from the other lockers, simply pretending to be ordinary.
Was that horrible thing I'd just seen really {f:inside|inside} it?{p}

"GYAAAAAAAAAAGH!"
A hideous scream came from inside.
It was Fukuzawa's voice.{p}

Back then, the captain of the girls' swim club was a girl named Yuko Seto.
She was a famous swimmer who held a whole bunch of records. She won on her own, of course, and she led this school to team championships again and again.
The school got so crazy about the girls' swim club that there was even a plan to build a new pool behind the new school building.{p}

The swim club did have a boys' side too, but their results were kind of so-so. They didn't have many members either, and they always had to practice while giving way to the girls.
The incident happened during the summer vacation of Seto's third year.
Seto already had a university recommendation lined up, so even after the other third-years retired from the club, she never missed practice.{p}

That day was clear and hot, they say.
On days like that, being in the water feels so good, doesn't it?
Unlike the girls, who were training like crazy for the meet after summer vacation, the boys seemed like they were mostly just having fun splashing around.{p}

They opened the pool gate and let the stray dog in.
They wanted to give Seto a scare.
She was always tearing into them and they never talked back, so it was meant as a little payback.{p}

They all screamed and scattered, they say.
As far as the boys were concerned, the plan was a success.
Watching those stuck-up girls run around squealing seemed funny, and kind of cute.{p}

Listen, {c}{f:|}.
No matter how good you are at the dog paddle, you can't do it in this pool.
If you trampled all over my sister's feelings after everything she did...{p}

Hee hee hee, I wonder what I'd do~.
...Well, that's the end of my story.
On to the next person.{p}

That's right, people started hearing someone swimming in the pool when nobody was there.
Splash, splash, like that.
And you know, when that happens...{p}

Splash, splash.
Soft at first, then louder.
Until it sounded like someone drowning...{p}

It wasn't Seto who'd been holding a hand up out of the pool water.
What shocked Hayashi was that she saw a girl who looked exactly like her, reaching out from under the water.
The figure was wearing a sailor uniform, and it was translucent, wavering back and forth.{p}

...Girls are scary{f:, you know.|, aren't they?}
You shouldn't read everything in the best possible light.
Especially in a club that's all girls, all kinds of things go on{f:.|, you know.}
Maybe you wouldn't understand, {c}{f:|}.
{f:You're not a girl, after all.|Maybe you've never been through anything like that.}
...
Oh well, never mind.
Okay, I'll end my story here.
Who's next?
What kind of story will they tell us...?{p}

There was no one behind her.
Not just behind her; there was no one in the lanes next to her either.
Hayashi was the only one in the pool...{p}

There was nothing there.
And the pulling, which had been so strong, suddenly stopped dead.
A dream...?{p}

But on Hayashi's ankle, there was a clear handprint.
When she saw it, Hayashi hurriedly got out of the pool, threw on her clothes, and went home.
On the way, she passed some of the club members, but she didn't say a word and left as if she were running away, they say.{p}

"Huh, I must've imagined it."
The meet's coming up, so I'm just a little oversensitive, that's all.
She told herself that and started swimming again.{p}

Hayashi couldn't stand their stares and ducked under the water.
She shut her eyes and stayed under as long as her breath would hold.
As long as her breath would hold... so two or three minutes at most, I guess.{p}

What {f:could|could} be in the locker Seto supposedly used, now?
Since it's off-limits, maybe there's nothing in it at all{f:?|?}
"What are you thinking so hard about, {c}{f:|}?"
Fukuzawa peered into {f:my|my} face.
"Hey, which locker are we opening next?"{p}

"Stop it, {c}{f:|}..."
She looked like she was about to cry.
Maybe I teased her too much.
"Sorry, that was a lie{f:.|.}
I don't think this is any cursed locker{f:.|.}
The whole cursed locker thing might just be something somebody made up.
Let's hurry, open the other lockers, and get back to the club room."{p}

Okay, {f:two to go|just two left}.
We've come this far, so there's nothing for it but to open every last one{f:.|.}
Which one should I open next...?{p}

"..."
There was nothing inside.
............{p}

"{f:Hm|Huh}?
The door's {f:stuck|stuck}?"
The locker wouldn't budge, as if it were locked.{p}

"...{c}{f:|}, you can quit the act."
Fukuzawa frowned.
But it wasn't an act.{p}

"Fine, I'll open it!"
Fukuzawa reached out her hand.
And then...{p}

With the two of {f:us|us} pulling, the door came half open.
{f:But|But} it only opened for an instant.
That was because something inside slammed the locker shut{f:.|.}{p}

...Let's go back to the newspaper club.
And hear the sixth person's story{f:.|.}
We've come this far, there's no backing out now.
{f:We|We} walked in silence.{p}

When we got back to the newspaper club, the stuffy air greeted {f:us|us}.
{f:I|I} took a breath, then decided to hear the sixth story.
What kind of story was waiting for {f:me|me} this time, {f:I wonder|I wonder}...{p}

I just started running.
I had to get away.
Away from this cursed club room.{p}

"Gh... gah..."
My voice wouldn't come.
I can't breathe...{p}

Something like a cold hand touched my body.
But I couldn't turn around.
My neck was caught tight in the door.{p}

Then I noticed he'd already strode off ahead.
"W-wait, please."
I hurried after him.{p}
